---
import { appConfig } from "../app-config";
---

<section class="amanah sec geo" id="amanah" data-od-id="founding-amanah" aria-label="Founding amanah pledge">
  <div class="wrap amanah-grid">
    <div class="amanah-copy reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Before you reserve</span>
      <h2>A founding pledge, written with <span class="it">amanah.</span></h2>
      <p>Before paying for early access, you should know the promise clearly: what you reserve, what stays private, and which Islamic choices remain in your hands.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="covenant reveal d1">
      <div class="cov-head">
        <span class="pledge-seal" lang="ar" dir="rtl">أمانة</span>
        <strong>What your {appConfig.pricing.lifetimePrice} reserves</strong>
        <small>Founding lifetime access, held in trust until launch</small>
      </div>
      <ol class="cov-list">
        <li>
          <span class="cov-num" lang="ar" dir="rtl" aria-hidden="true">١</span>
          <p><b>No subscription, ever.</b> One payment at the founding price locks in lifetime access — not another monthly bill quietly renewing.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="cov-num" lang="ar" dir="rtl" aria-hidden="true">٢</span>
          <p><b>First through the door.</b> The day Barakah opens, you receive the launch email and your founding access instructions.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="cov-num" lang="ar" dir="rtl" aria-hidden="true">٣</span>
          <p><b>Your salah settings stay yours.</b> Prayer method, madhhab preference, qibla and locked apps are designed to stay private and controllable.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="cov-num" lang="ar" dir="rtl" aria-hidden="true">٤</span>
          <p><b>No fiqh claims.</b> Barakah does not issue rulings. It gives you the controls, then steps aside.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <div class="cov-foot"><span lang="ar" dir="rtl">أمانة</span> — a trust, held carefully until it is returned.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
